  "notes": "Closed-score SATB: Soprano+Alto share the treble staff, Tenor+Bass share the bass staff. A correct conversion yields FOUR parts (Soprano, Alto, Tenor, Bass), each with its own notes; all three verses belong to the Soprano part (lyric numbers 1-3) and must stay attached to soprano notes, including melisma skips (e.g. \"pre - cious\" spans a slurred melisma). DAMAGE (halftone): Page reproduced through a clustered-dot halftone screen (offset reprint of a photo of the page) and re-scanned by point sampling, giving moire: every stroke and the paper tone are made of dots. mild 150 lpi/45 deg, scan 110 lpi/15 deg with 0.97 rescale, severe 85 lpi/30 deg, 18% paper tone, 0.93 rescale + 0.7 deg rotation and JPEG 50. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: The 0.97 / 0.93 rescale makes the music slightly smaller than the page (centred)."
